        <hr noshade size="1">
        
        <font color="#000000" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2"> Well, I have removed myself from the guild.  I have just felt a need for change.  Right now, I feel alone when I log in.  I usually say hello to the guild, then go off in Seb or KC, turn on LFG.  When I find a group, it is often a pick up group, which are just not my favorite (though they can be good groups, they are often not). I guess I am looking for a wider pool of people who are of similar level for adventures into some of the higher level zones.  Experience with the people you group with goes a long ways in making a group more efficient and more fun, but pickup groups don't often yield this benefit.</P><P>I do much enjoy the company of most everyone in the guild, but the oppurtunities to group up in challenging situations just don't often present themselves with the current disparity in levels amongst the guild members. </P><P>I do consider you all to still be my friends, and hope you will call on me if you ever have need of a train pulling monk, help with an epic mob, or whatever.  I will certainly be around, and will still be looking out for you all, in fact, the first hot key I made after leaving, was a /who all "lore keepers" one.</P><P>Best wishes to you all and see you in game,</P><P>Chakar<BR>56th Master<BR>Swifttail of the Fourth Rung<BR>Follower of Glox</font></td>
